      "name": "CreateGameObject",
      "signature": "void * CreateGameObject(dword dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a game object with specified flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if flag 0x2 is set; if so, call initialization check function\n2. If initialization check fails, return without allocation\n3. Check flags 0x2 and 0x1 to determine allocation path\n4. Allocate 96-byte buffer from memory pool\n5. Zero-initialize 24 dwords (96 bytes) via REP STOSD\n6. Call object initialization with allocated buffer and input flags\n7. If initialization succeeds, register object and return pointer\n8. On failure, free buffer and return NULL\n\nParameters:\n- dwFlags (dword): Bit flags controlling object allocation (0x1, 0x2)\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to allocated and initialized game object, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60 (96): Object allocation size in bytes\n- 0x18: Number of dwords to zero (24 dwords = 96 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
