      "name": "QueueSoundBuffer",
      "signature": "void QueueSoundBuffer(void * pSoundUnit, dword dwData, int nTimeout)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Queues a sound buffer for playback with timeout.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify pSoundUnit is not NULL via FogAssert\n2. Call Ordinal_10002 to check if sound system is initialized\n3. If initialized, acquire critical section lock for thread safety\n4. Set buffer status to queued (1) at offset 0x4c\n5. Copy reference from offset 0x38 to 0x50\n6. Store sound data parameter at offset 0x54\n7. Get current tick count and store at offset 0x58\n8. Calculate and store expiration (current + timeout) at 0x5c\n9. Release critical section lock and return\n\nParameters:\n- pSoundUnit (void*): Sound unit structure, cannot be NULL\n- dwData (dword): Sound data to queue for playback\n- nTimeout (int): Timeout duration in milliseconds\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:5",
