      "name": "SetSampleValue",
      "signature": "void SetSampleValue(void * this, float flNewValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the sample value for this sound object and triggers notification if conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate this pointer is non-null (abort with FogAssert if NULL)\n2. Store flNewValue in object field at offset 0x3c (sample value)\n3. Check if object has callback at offset 0x10\n4. If callback exists and GetGlobalFlag() returns 2:\n   a. Check if byte at offset 0x34 has bit 2 set OR flNewValue equals g_flMaxSoundLevel\n   b. Calculate attenuation delta: g_ldDefaultSoundLevel - flNewValue\n   c. Convert result to integer via __ftol()\n   d. Invoke virtual callback with calculated delta\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Pointer to sound sample object (ECX, __thiscall)\n- flNewValue (float): New sample value to set\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c: Offset of sample value field in object\n- 0x10: Offset of callback interface pointer\n- 0x34: Offset of control flags byte\n- 0x04: Bit mask for notification enable flag\n- 0x02: Global flag value indicating notifications enabled\n- 0x07: Notification type constant passed to callback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:4",
