      "name": "ProcessAudioEvent",
      "signature": "void ProcessAudioEvent(void * this, void * pAudioObject, float flVolume)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes audio event with volume parameter and updates audio state management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pAudioObject pointer (asserts on NULL, calls FUN_6f9e5965)\n2. Query audio system status via GetEaxStatus()\n3. If status is inactive, reset flVolume to 0.0\n4. Check if context pointer at offset 0x10 is valid\n5. If valid: retrieve global flag state via GetGlobalFlag()\n6. If flag equals 1: queue audio event with status code 1 and g_guidDestinationID\n7. Otherwise: clamp flVolume via Ordinal_10054(0.0, 1.0, flVolume)\n8. Convert result to integer via __ftol() and queue with status code 5\n9. Push context to audio queue with g_guidSourceID and additional parameters\n10. Execute pending audio operations via virtual method at offset 0x10\n\nParameters:\n- pAudioObject (void *): Audio processing object instance\n- flVolume (float): Desired volume level (0.0-1.0 range)\n\nReturns:\n- void (state modified via side effects to audio context)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10: Offset to audio context pointer\n- 0x34d: Source line number (assertion reference)\n- 1: Active/enabled flag value\n- 5: Default event status code",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
