      "name": "StartBackgroundMusicPlayback",
      "signature": "void StartBackgroundMusicPlayback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize and start audio playback for background music.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section for thread safety\n2. Validate audio game object and audio device state\n3. Initialize music intro flag if needed\n4. Clear or populate audio stream pointers based on intro flag\n5. Select random or fixed music track from available streams\n6. Open audio stream and set sound volume to 0x6E (110)\n7. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure\n8. Leave critical section\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Global g_pAudioGameObject (audio device handle)\n- IMPLICIT: Global g_hSoundCriticalSection (thread synchronization)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if audio stream opened successfully\n- 0 if audio device invalid or stream open failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6E (110): Default sound volume level\n- 0x00: Music intro disabled flag\n- Multiple globals: DAT_6f9f3d20 (intro flag cache), DAT_6f9f0830 (stream count), DAT_6f9f3d18 (track selection)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
