      "comment": "Reads PE file data into buffer, validating file format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Open file for reading with CreateFileA\n2. Create file mapping via CreateFileMappingA\n3. Map file view into memory\n4. Validate MZ header magic (0x5A4D)\n5. Locate PE header and validate PE magic (0x454C)\n6. Check section count (piSectionHeader[0x2f]) is non-zero\n7. Get data size from piSectionHeader[0x2e] offset + 8\n8. If buffer too small, set required size and return ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_BUFFER\n9. Clear destination buffer (DWORD-aligned then byte remainder)\n10. Copy data from file (DWORD-aligned then byte remainder)\n11. Set error code to 0 on success, return 1\n\nParameters:\n- szFilePath (LPCSTR): Path to PE executable file\n- pdwSize (dword*): Buffer size on input, required size on output\n- pdwBuffer (dword*): Destination buffer for file data\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5A4D (21581): MZ header magic number\n- 0x454C (17740): PE header magic number (little-endian EL)\n- 0x1E: Offset in MZ header to PE header offset\n- 0x2E, 0x2F: Section header offsets within PE header\n- 0x80000000: GENERIC_READ file access\n- 0x714, 0x7A: Windows error codes",
