      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts a 64-bit floating point value to string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract integer part from double value using bit manipulation\n2. Convert double to string with proper decimal point placement\n3. Add sign character if negative\n4. Format final string with proper null termination\n\nParameters:\n- pdblValue (double*): Pointer to 64-bit float value\n- szBuffer (char*): Output string buffer\n- nSize (size_t): Maximum buffer size\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to szBuffer (output string)",
