      "signature": "void FUN_6fd23482(double * pdblValue, char * szBuffer, size_t nSize, int nFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats a double value into a string buffer with appropriate precision and notation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract double into integer components via FUN_6f9e835a (sign, exponent)\n2. Initialize output string with FUN_6f9e82e3 to handle sign prefix\n3. Determine if value requires exponential vs fixed-point notation\n4. If exponent is out of range (-4 to buffer size):\n   - Call FormatFloatingPointExponent for scientific notation (e.g., 1.23e-10)\n5. Otherwise for fixed-point notation:\n   - Find string null terminator\n   - Truncate extra digits if needed\n   - Call FUN_6f9e64d1 to apply final format\n\nParameters:\n- pdblValue (double*): Pointer to double value to convert\n- szBuffer (char*): Output string buffer (minimum 65 bytes recommended)\n- nSize (size_t): Size of output buffer in bytes\n- nFormat (int): Format specifier (0x65='e' or 0x66='f' for exp/fixed)\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in szBuffer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:466e27d82e265155c21adbf5b42c1734",
