      "name": "ClassifyFloatAsIntegerType",
      "signature": "int ClassifyFloatAsIntegerType(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Classifies a float10 value in ST0 as integer type for exponent handling.\n\nUsed by Exp2F64 to determine special case handling for 2^x computation.\nTests if the value in ST0 is an integer and if so, whether it's even or odd.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Round ST0 to nearest integer using FRNDINT\n2. Compare rounded value with original ST0\n3. If not equal (not an integer), return 0\n4. If integer, multiply by 0.5 (g_dHalf) to test parity\n5. Round the halved value and compare with original halved value\n6. If equal (value*0.5 is integer, meaning value is even), return 2\n7. If not equal (value is odd integer), return 1\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT: in_ST0 (float10) - Value to classify (exponent from Exp2F64)\n\nReturns:\nint - Classification result:\n  0 = Not an integer (fractional exponent)\n  1 = Odd integer exponent\n  2 = Even integer exponent\n\nGlobals Referenced:\ng_dHalf (0x6f9f0d02) - Constant 0.5 for parity test\n\nCalled By:\nExp2F64 - Uses result to select special case computation path",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:df587a37c8639f83cd433c3a3fbdafc4",
