      "name": "FpuExchangeAndPop",
      "signature": "void FpuExchangeAndPop(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exchanges the top two elements of the FPU stack and pops the top element\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Exchange the top two FPU stack elements (ST0 <-> ST1)\n2. Store and pop the current top element (originally ST1)\n\nParameters:\n  None - operates directly on FPU stack\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies FPU stack state only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - FPU stack must contain at least two elements before calling\n  - Result leaves the original ST1 value as new ST0, original ST0 is discarded\n  - Used in floating-point arithmetic cleanup operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
