      "name": "ComputePowerOfTwo",
      "signature": "float10 * ComputePowerOfTwo(float10 ldExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Computes 2^x (2 raised to the power x) using extended precision floating point arithmetic\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Duplicate input exponent on FPU stack for integer/fraction separation\n2. Round input to integer (FRNDINT) for integer part extraction  \n3. Subtract integer part from original to get fractional part (FSUBR)\n4. Exchange stack positions to process fractional part (FXCH)\n5. Negate fractional part for F2XM1 instruction compatibility (FCHS)\n6. Compute 2^fractional_part - 1 using F2XM1 instruction\n7. Add 1.0 to complete 2^fractional_part calculation (FLD1, FADDP)\n8. Scale result by 2^integer_part using FSCALE instruction\n9. Clean up FPU stack and return extended precision result\n\nParameters:\nldExponent - Extended precision floating point exponent value (passed via FPU stack ST0)\n\nReturns:\nExtended precision floating point result of 2^ldExponent\nResult computed with full 80-bit precision using x86 FPU instructions\n\nSpecial Cases:\nF2XM1 instruction requires input in range [-1, +1] for accurate results\nFSCALE provides exact scaling for integer powers of 2\nFunction preserves maximum precision throughout calculation chain\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\nNo magic constants - uses FPU built-in constants (1.0 from FLD1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3f015c1c75c5efb05d68ef52e0407e8b",
