      "name": "SetFpuControlWord",
      "signature": "void SetFpuControlWord(uint dwControl)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures the x87 FPU control word for extended precision floating-point operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load FPU control flags parameter from stack [ESP + 0x4]\n2. Extract rounding mode bits using mask 0x300 (bits 10-11)\n3. Combine with precision control 0x7f (64-bit mantissa + exception masks)\n4. Store modified control word to stack temporary location\n5. Load new control word into FPU using FLDCW instruction\n\nParameters:\nwFpuControlFlags (ushort): FPU control flags containing rounding mode in bits 10-11\n  IMPLICIT: Function receives parameter through stack despite void signature\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function modifies FPU state directly, no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Preserves only rounding mode from input flags (bits 10-11)\n- Forces extended precision mode (0x300 masked to 0x200)\n- Enables all exception masks for robust calculation\n- Temporary storage on stack at [ESP + 0x6] for FLDCW instruction\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x300 (768): Rounding mode bit mask (RC field bits 10-11)\n0x7f (127): Exception mask + precision control (53-bit mantissa, all exceptions masked)\n\nFPU Control Word Bit Layout:\nBit  Purpose           Value Set\n0-5  Exception Masks   111111 (all masked)\n6-7  Reserved          00\n8-9  Precision Control 11 (extended precision)\n10-11 Rounding Control Preserved from input parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
