      "name": "HandleExtendedPrecisionFpuException",
      "signature": "void HandleExtendedPrecisionFpuException(float10 * pflResult, uint dwErrorCode, ushort wControlWord, uint dwContext1, uint dwContext2, uint dwContext3, uint dwContext4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles FPU exceptions for extended precision floating-point operations with scaling and error propagation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract high dword from input extended precision value to check exponent\n2. Check for denormal numbers (exponent = 0): scale with scaling constant 1\n3. Check for infinity/NaN (exponent = 0x7FF): scale with scaling constant 2  \n4. Validate FPU status and control word state for proper operation\n5. Branch to specialized error handling based on error code (0x1D = extended precision prep)\n6. Call appropriate error handler with context parameters\n\nParameters:\n  pflResult: Extended precision float pointer to store result/error value\n  dwErrorCode: Error code indicating exception type (0x1D = extended precision call)\n  wControlWord: FPU control word for precision/rounding mode\n  dwContext1-dwContext4: Error context data passed to handlers\n  IMPLICIT: ldInputValue in ST0 register contains source floating-point value\n  IMPLICIT: wFpuStatusWord contains current FPU exception flags\n\nReturns:\n  void - Result stored at pflResult location or passed to error handlers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Denormal input (exponent = 0): Scaled using constant at 0x100283ec\n  - Infinity/NaN input (exponent = 0x7FF): Scaled using constant at 0x100283e4\n  - Control word validation failure: Early return without processing\n  - Error code 0x1D: Routed to PrepareExtendedPrecisionFpuCall\n  - Other error codes: Routed to __startOneArgErrorHandling\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7ff0000000000000: IEEE 754 exponent mask for double precision\n  0x7ff00000: Exponent mask for high dword  \n  0x27f: FPU control word validation constant\n  0x20: FPU precision exception bit mask\n  0x1d: Extended precision call error code\n  0x100283ec: Denormal scaling constant address\n  0x100283e4: Infinity/NaN scaling constant address\n  0x100283dc: Comparison threshold for scaled values\n  0x100283fc: Multiplication factor for small values  \n  0x100283d4: Comparison threshold for infinity cases\n  0x100283f4: Multiplication factor for large values\n\nError Handling:\n  - Invalid control word: Silent return\n  - FPU exception pending: Silent return  \n  - Extended precision error (0x1D): Delegates to PrepareExtendedPrecisionFpuCall\n  - General FPU errors: Delegates to __startOneArgErrorHandling",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
