      "name": "GetFpuStatusWord",
      "signature": "int GetFpuStatusWord(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current floating-point unit status word and clears pending exceptions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up stack frame and allocate space for FPU status word\n2. Store FPU status word to local stack variable using FNSTSW instruction\n3. Clear all pending FPU exceptions using FNCLEX instruction\n4. Load status word from stack and sign-extend to 32-bit integer\n5. Return the status word as signed integer\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - FPU status word containing exception flags and control information\n     Bits 0-5: Exception flags (IE, DE, ZE, OE, UE, PE)\n     Bits 6-7: Stack fault flags\n     Bits 8-10: Condition code bits C0-C2\n     Bits 11-13: Stack top pointer (TOP)\n     Bit 14: Condition code bit C3\n     Bit 15: FPU busy flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction clears all pending FPU exceptions before returning status word.\nReturn value is sign-extended from 16-bit to 32-bit integer.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xFFFF - Maximum 16-bit value (status word mask)\n\nError Handling:\nNo error conditions - FPU status word retrieval always succeeds.\nFNCLEX instruction resets all exception flags to clear state.\n\nNote: Function uses 1 stack-allocated temporary variable optimized away by decompiler",
