      "name": "pow",
      "signature": "double pow(double base, double exponent, int param_3, uint param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "double",
      "comment": "Computes base raised to the power of exponent using IEEE 754 floating-point arithmetic.\nHandles special cases: NaN, infinity, zero, negative bases, and denormal numbers.\nReturns double-precision result via FPU stack.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save and validate current FPU control word\n2. Check exponent for NaN/infinity cases\n3. Check base for special values (zero, NaN, infinity)\n4. Handle negative base with log2-based power computation\n5. For normal bases: compute base^exponent using FYL2X and 2^x\n6. Handle fractional exponents via __powhlp for integer test\n7. Apply sign correction based on base sign and exponent parity\n8. Return result on FPU stack, restore FPU state\n\nParameters:\n  baseHi (EAX/param_1): Upper 32 bits of base (double)\n  baseLo (param_2): Lower 32 bits of base (double)\n  exponentHi (param_3): Upper 32 bits of exponent (double)\n  exponentLo (param_4): Lower 32 bits of exponent (double)\n\nReturns:\n  ST0: Result of base^exponent as extended double-precision float\n  EAX: Status code (0=normal, 1=special case, 2=infinity result, 7=nan result)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - base=0, exponent>0: returns 0\n  - base=0, exponent<=0: returns infinity or NaN\n  - base=1: returns 1 for any exponent\n  - base<0, non-integer exponent: returns NaN\n  - base=infinity: returns 0 or infinity based on exponent sign\n  - Negative exponents: 1/base^|exponent|\n  - Denormal numbers: handled via SetupFloatingPointExceptionContext",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
