      "name": "ComputeBaseToExponentPower",
      "signature": "int ComputeBaseToExponentPower(int pResultStorage, double dBase, int iExponentInteger)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Computes base^exponent using IEEE 754 double precision with table-driven mantissa approximation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract IEEE 754 exponent and mantissa components via bit shifting (right shift by 44 bits for exponent extraction)\n2. Perform initial table lookup using mantissa normalization index from g_dMantissaTableBase (offset by uintTableIndex*4)\n3. Validate exponent range [0x10, 0x7fef); jump to special case handling if outside normal range\n4. For normal case: enter main mantissa processing loop executing iterative table-driven polynomial approximation\n5. Extract secondary exponent field via right shift by 38 bits and lookup scaling coefficients from g_dSecondaryMantissaTable\n6. Perform second-level table lookup with refined index via g_dTertiaryScalingTable and accumulate polynomial terms\n7. Refine mantissa using polynomial coefficients (g_dPolynomialCoeff1 through g_dPolynomialCoeff5) with iterative multiplication\n8. Accumulate scaled exponent contribution from lookup tables (g_dExponentAdjustmentTable, g_dExponentRefinementTable)\n9. Compute final result using accumulated mantissa and exponent with 128.0 scaling factor (0x4060)\n10. Validate result mantissa via bounds check against 0x1ff7f (upper) and -0x1e1ff (lower) with underflow/overflow detection\n11. Apply underflow (result < min double) or overflow (result > max double) handling returning normalized values\n12. Dispatch to DispatchMathematicalOperation with operation code in EDX for final IEEE rounding and special case handling\n\nParameters:\n- pResultStorage (int): Pointer to 80-bit extended precision storage for return value (x87 FPU format)\n- dBase (double): Base value in IEEE 754 double precision format; supports all floating-point classes\n- iExponentInteger (int): Integer component from parameter packing (unused in standard case, for edge case handling)\n- uiExponentHigh (uint): High-order 32 bits of exponent from parameter packing\n\nReturns:\n- float10 via x87 FPU: 80-bit extended precision result stored in x87 register ST0\n- Return values: normal finite results, infinity (base > 1 with large exponent), zero (base < 1 with large exponent)\n- Special cases: 0^0 = 1, 0^negative = infinity, 1^any = 1, negative_base^integer handled per sign\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero base with positive exponent: returns 0.0 (operation code 0x1a)\n- Zero base with negative/zero exponent: returns infinity (operation code 0x1d)\n- Base 1.0 with any exponent: returns 1.0 (special mantissa detection at offset 0x3ff00000)\n- Base -1.0 with even integer exponent: returns 1.0; with odd exponent: returns -1.0\n- Subnormal base values: normalized via scaling by 2^64 before main algorithm, restart loop\n- Subnormal exponent (exponent range [0x10, 0x7fef)): bounds validation at 0x6fc2dbb0-dbb6\n- NaN base: dispatched with operation code 0x3ee for IEEE special value handling\n- Infinity base: dispatched with operation codes 0x18-0x1d based on sign/exponent configuration\n- Overflow condition: result exponent exceeds 0x40a0, dispatch operation code 0x18 (infinity result)\n- Underflow condition: result exponent below 0x3c70, dispatch operation code 0x19 (zero/subnormal result)\n- Mantissa index bounds validation: index range [0x1ff7f, -0x1e1ff] at offset 0x6fc2dd83-dd99\n\nStructure Layout (IEEE 754 Double Precision):\nOffset    Size    Field Name              Type       Description\n0x00      8       Double Value            double     Full 64-bit IEEE 754 value\n0x00      1       Mantissa Bits [0:7]     byte       Low 8 bits of normalized mantissa\n0x04      4       Exponent+Sign [0:31]    uint       Bits [32:63]: exponent (11 bits) + sign (1 bit)\n0x06      2       Exponent Field [0:15]   ushort     Bits [52:62]: biased exponent (11 bits)\n0x07      1       Sign Bit                byte       Bit 63: sign (1=negative, 0=positive)",
